  "notes": [
    "HAND-TUNED 2026-09-02 to the 8-part ceiling for a walk-under bay: the derivation at 8 parts pruned the four posts and the two low rails into two 4 m WALLS along z (part layer3-1+layer2-0+layer1-1+layer1-3+layer0-0+layer0-2, 0.17 x 0.97 x 1.98 half-extents), which a player could not walk between; at --max-parts 14 it kept them apart but promote refuses 14. So: four 0.18 m post columns 0 to 1.95, one head-frame slab 1.95 to 2.19 over +-1.95, and the gable as three slabs (2.19-2.68 over the whole bay, 2.68-2.90 to z +-1.15, 2.90-3.10 to z +-0.35) whose tops sit on the roof surface at each band's inner edge, so no step overshoots the real surface by more than 0.24 m. The low z-rails (1.79-1.95 at x +-1.68) are not carried: a player passing a gable side clips a culm at head height rather than meeting an invisible wall."
